<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A3116004" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "02" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Front Drive Shaft Assembly Disassembly and Reassembly
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A3116001">Front Drive Shaft Components:Front</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A3116003">Front Drive Shaft Assembly Removal and Installation:Front</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A3116004009" page = "2">
<title>
Disassembly
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Disassembly of the wheel side joint in the left side drive shaft or the tripod joint can affect the performance.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If any abnormality is found, replace the drive shaft or the tripod joint(s) as an assembly.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<topic id = "AENLSB0A3116004010" page = "2">
<title>
Differential side joint
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Using nose pliers (1), disengage hooks of boot big band (2) and remove band.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEL10A311006.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "55.149mm" ver = "01" gw = "196" gh = "139"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove differential side joint housing from tripod joint.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
For right side drive shaft, remove drive shaft support bracket (1) and washer (2) from differential side joint housing, if necessary.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IHSB0A311009.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "75.427mm" ver = "01" gw = "199" gh = "197"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Wipe off grease from shaft and use snap ring pliers (2) to remove snap ring (1).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I7RW01311003.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "49.561mm" ver = "01" gw = "95" gh = "123"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove tripod joint (1) using 3-arm puller (2).
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Except for the housing, washing the tripod joint parts with a washing solution may cause problems with the joint.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not use a washing solution to clean any tripod joint parts other than the housing. Use a cloth to remove grease from tripod joints.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I9P60A311005.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "42.746mm" ver = "01" gw = "173" gh = "105"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Using flat-bladed screwdriver (1) or the like, release caulking (2) of boot small band (3).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I8V101311031.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "38.286mm" ver = "01" gw = "172" gh = "92"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Pull out differential side boot from shaft.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
For right side drive shaft, remove damper from shaft.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</topic>
<topic id = "AENLSB0A3116004011" page = "2">
<title>
Wheel side joint
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Wheel side joint assembly in the right side drive shaft cannot be disassembled.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If any abnormality is found, replace the joint as an assembly.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
For left side drive shaft, using flat-bladed screwdriver (1) or the like, release caulking (2) of boot small band (3) and big band (4).
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Use nippers to cut boot band if it is of a welded type.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Take care not to damage boot while cutting band.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<figure page = "2">
<graphic graphicname = "IFFA0A311002.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "48.701mm" ver = "01" gw = "170" gh = "122"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Pull out wheel side boot from shaft.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</topic>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A3116004012" page = "2">
<title>
Reassembly
</title>
<ptxt>
Judging from abnormality noted before disassembly and what is found through visual check of component parts after disassembly, prepare replacing parts and proceed to reassembly.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Check that wheel side joint assembly (1) and differential side joint housing (2) are washed thoroughly and air-dried.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Inadequate or insufficient lubricant will reduce durability of the joint.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Lubricate each joint with specified amount of specified grease following instructions shown below.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
If removed joint boot(s) (3) is to be reused, wiping off of the inside grease with shop cloth is recommended.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<figure page = "2">
<graphic graphicname = "I4RS0A310007.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "77.712mm" ver = "01" gw = "184" gh = "203"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
